From: slwyts <slwyts@foxmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm: apply SDR color management consistently without plane LUTs

MSM lacks the AMD plane color pipeline. Direct scanout skipped the SDR LUT
while cursor composition applied it, changing colors with the input device.
Use shader color management whenever the display backend cannot apply it.
Disabling color management still permits direct scanout.

--- a/src/Backends/DRMBackend.cpp
+++ b/src/Backends/DRMBackend.cpp
@@ -4657,7 +4657,13 @@
 			else
 			{
 				if ( !SupportsColorManagement() )
+				{
+					// Scanout has no plane LUTs on this backend. Preserve the
+					// same SDR gamut, gamma and night-mode transform whether
+					// a cursor/overlay happens to require composition or not.
+					bNeedsFullComposite |= pFrameInfo->applyOutputColorMgmt;
 					bNeedsFullComposite |= ColorspaceIsHDR( pFrameInfo->layers.get( 0 ).colorspace );
+				}
 			}
 
 			bNeedsFullComposite |= !!(g_uCompositeDebug & CompositeDebugFlag::Heatmap);
